# Resume tailoring

- Source of truth: `master/resume.tex` (etoolbox toggles at the top). Do not edit it unless asked to update the master. Copy `master/resume.example.tex` if you do not have one yet.
- Extra facts / toggle table: `master/bank.md` (from `master/bank.example.md`). New bullets are allowed from the bank. Do not invent tools.
- Long papers stay on disk. Index is the bank. Optional paths: `.cursor/skills/tailor-resume/sources.md`.
- If `.cursor/skills/tailor-resume/SKILL.local.md` exists, follow it for private constraints.
- When the user pastes a job description, pastes application/job URLs, asks to tailor/apply, or asks for a cover letter: follow `.cursor/skills/tailor-resume/SKILL.md`.
- After compile, run `python3 .cursor/skills/tailor-resume/scripts/check_resume.py applications/{slug}`. Italic project headings must not shove the date. If GPU names are already in a project's bullets, do not also put them on the italic heading.
- For URLs, scrape first with `python3 .cursor/skills/tailor-resume/scripts/scrape_jd.py URL`. Never invent a JD.
- Never launch GStack Browser. Never run `$B connect`, `$B handoff`, `$B --headed`, or the gstack `/browse` skill. Job pages: `scrape_jd.py`, `harvest_apply_form.py` (headless), then WebFetch. Login wall or CAPTCHA: write visible fields or None found and stop.
- Write each version to `applications/{company}-{role}/` (`resume.tex`, `job.md`, `application_questions.md`, `{First}_{Last}_resume.pdf` from `profile.json`, optional `cover_letter.md`). After compile, `cp resume.pdf First_Last_resume.pdf`. Never ship a tailored PDF named only `resume.pdf`.
- Cover letters are opt-in (dashboard **Make cover letter**, add-job checkbox, or asking in chat). Follow `.cursor/skills/tailor-resume/writing.md`. Personal bank scene with cause and effect, realistic intern depth, off-resume material. No citizenship/relocation in letters. No em dashes, no colon-lists, no stacked punchy short sentences.
- When scraping a posting, also scrape apply-form questions and draft answers. If the form is not on the listing, click Start Application / Apply (never Submit). Never invent work auth, visa, or EEO data.
- Keep tailored resumes to **one full page**. A short one-pager is a failed tailor. Keep each line full: if a bullet, skills row, or coursework line wraps and leaves only a word or two, cut so those words fit on the line above, or add true content so the last line is nearly full.
- Match as many true JD keywords as possible. Education stays at the top. Default Yale degree is Computer Science (`showmolbio` off); turn the toggle on only when the role itself is biology / biotech / computational biology. Jobs and projects stay reverse chronological; Skills / Experience / Projects sections may be swapped as wholes.
- Track and Tailor daily watcher for SimplifyJobs listings: `automation/` (`make internships-install`, `make internships-now`). Tailors with Cursor Agent CLI. After compile, Python (`check_resume.py`) must see exactly one page; the watcher retries the agent on overflow.
